+# ECON-03a — Resource-only interactive world boundary
+
+**Baseline:** ECON-02B2d18d Shared NPC Duties source archive.  
+**Scope:** remove active station-market issuance/trading and visible financial controls from normal game host while retaining archived pre-change fixture tests.
+
+## Code
+
+- `Simulation::spawn_ship_docked(..., legacy_wallet)` allows an explicitly resource-only initial-world spawn without an even-zero wallet entry. Existing B5/B6 test callers remain backward compatible.
+- `build_lumen_reach(..., legacy_station_markets)` makes the old seed-market setup opt-in to this caller; extra systems remain discoverable without minted currency reserves.
+- `galaxy_interactive_host` defaults to no markets and no wallet. It declines `SELL` even from stdin. `--legacy-market-fixture` only works in builds that compile `SG_QA_AUTOMATION`, preserving historical regression worlds without silently reviving the commercial market in production.
+- The local relay exposes the legacy fixture flag only for explicit developer tests. Default `/session` omits `sell` capabilities, rejects `sell` requests, and preserves token/origin checks and resource movement commands.
+- The browser hides market/sale widgets unless `/session` identifies a historical testing fixture. The old wire frame parser and archived recordings can still be inspected.
+- Existing archived B5/B6 trading regression scripts explicitly select the legacy fixture. The player-facing resource-only rules are documented in `docs/design/RESOURCE_ECONOMY_INVITE_ONLY_AND_FUTURE_MMO_2026-11-01.md`.
+
+## Important limitations
+
+- `SellOre`, `StationMarket`, `wallets_`, credit-journal readers, and old wire records remain in the kernel/persistence layer for archived compatibility and historical tests. Do **not** interpret this milestone as a whole-kernel financial-code deletion.
+- The established `galaxy_colony_live_host` was already resource-driven with no seeded stations/markets; this milestone primarily removes the old station-demo defaults.
+- A new invite-only multiplayer transport, invitation UI, 3D engine, and fully integrated NPC deliveries are **not** implemented here.
+- No production Windows build or full historical CTest suite acceptance is claimed.
+
+## Verification evidence
+
+- CMake/Ninja built `galaxy_interactive_host`, `galaxy_colony_live_host`, and four relevant native regression executables.
+- `ECON03aResourceOnlyHostTests.py`: direct default game and archived fixture, authenticated HTTP, forged token rejection, default no-sell API and hidden UI.
+- CTest focused run: 7/7 passed: kernel, B5.2 station, B5.3 logistics and live, resource-only, B6.2c projection and B6.4 region.
+- Node suite `node --test tests/*.js`: 93/93 passed.
+- `B53InteractiveEndToEndTests.py` archived fixture 2/2 passes.
+- Full all-target build attempt was interrupted by its execution window during compilation (52/188 build steps logged); this is **not** a full build success claim.
+
+## Next
+
+1. Isolate old market schema/credit journal in historical adapters without corrupting legacy saves. Define an explicit migration path rather than erasing users' data.
+2. Finish physical NPC delivery to generic factory machine ports and reconcile aggregate labor accounting.
+3. Continue visual/playability vertical-slice acceptance; do not substitute protocol or backend tests for actual game feel.
